<article class="env-definition" id="047D">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/047D">Definition <span data-tag="047D">39.4.3</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme. Let $(G, m)$ be a group scheme over $S$. </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
A <em>closed subgroup scheme</em> of $G$ is a closed subscheme $H \subset G$ such that $m|_{H \times _ S H}$ factors through $H$ and induces a group scheme structure on $H$ over $S$. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
An <em>open subgroup scheme</em> of $G$ is an open subscheme $G' \subset G$ such that $m|_{G' \times _ S G'}$ factors through $G'$ and induces a group scheme structure on $G'$ over $S$. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article>